alking to as many  alumni current students as possible to  hear about their  individual experiences at their  individual business schools will help  guide you  in terms of deciding where to apply and  then ultimately where you go  i would go back to what i had mentioned  earlier which is this idea of  authenticity and  you know if you're given this group is  really thinking about the application  process  and you know this concern around will i  be quantitative enough or  will i be able to transition into the  right job it's really about showing  the admissions team who you are what you  care about  um not trying to present what you think  people are looking for because  we probably have and had no idea what  they're actually looking for we just  know what we  care about and by showing that  it's going to determine your best match  um the best match for you and so  really taking the time to sit with  yourself and figuring out what that is  for you  and then authentically translating that  um and you know we talked about  recommendations finding someone who  really knows you  not sort of someone who you think may be  impressive but not know you very well  i would imagine that it's more impactful  someone who can really tell your story  has really  worked with you in some capacity um so  just to  feel like when you're turning over that  application you're like this is me  um you know when helen had said that i  had never heard this the story about the  printer but the first thought when you  started saying that about like someone  finding the printer  i think the other side to that is like  someone picks it up and your name isn't  on there and they know that's you  right not like you know that could be  the other side equation something  personal but also like if i picked it up  and  no one knows who it is like but someone  knows you're like oh that's so you  and and finding that in yourself and  then being able to translate that  because  the school will respond to you know your  mat your match in terms of school will i  think come out that way  um and then once you're there um  having that same attitude of sort of  really showing up and being present  being open to all kinds of things and  really  not going into it with preconceived  notions about how you should  show up or shouldn't show up but really  just being open to it your classmates  are going to be amazing  um you're going to learn so much from  everyone around you and just sort of  being in sponge mode i think  it's it's something that i miss most  about  um sort of having laughter the community  is just  you just get to be a sponge all day it's  an amazing experience  um ally or natalie's any final  yeah i i can go nuts i i i really  completely with andrew was saying um  about authenticity and what i would add  to that is  the reflection i made when writing what  matters most to you and why  was really really valuable to me  personally so i would think of it as  like  broader than this application it's an  opportunity for you to think about your  life holistically  put a thread to your experiences and  really think about  what you want to get out of the next  five years 10 years  and i found myself using that reflection  quite a bit during my time at gsb and  even today in classes when i think about  my values and  so it's it's more than just an essay  it's an opportunity for you to have some  very valuable  self-reflection  um i'll say i'll add two things one is  if you're  thinking about applying but you're not  sure if this is you know the right path  for you  i will say that for me personally gsp  changed my life full stop  um in terms of my friends  um and certainly you know some uh  relationships that  um i really value um  and and just how i i operate in the  world how i think about um the future  um and how i want to make an impact  um number two i would say that for  untraditional applicants  i think and i think this is sort of what  other people have said  um but i think it's important so if you  do get in that  you're strategic about where you  um about where you want to go if it  in terms of whether it's three years  from now or five years from now  and sort of let that be sort of a  um an influence in how you  um how you navigate your journey  at the gsb um because i think that it's  more required i think for an  untraditional  applicant than for someone who's going  to return  to their industry  amazing thank you thank my all of our  panelists for joining us today  and taking time out of your busy  schedules thanks for those who were able  to  sit in and join us today um if you have  any questions  feel free to email our office anytime  always available for you  for you and you can always check our  website for  future events um and staying connected  with us so thanks so much and have a  great day
 

